fix: do not advertise 10-bit plane formats

DrmFormat2CBiosFormat() only maps ARGB2101010; the XRGB/XBGR/ABGR
2101010 formats fall through to A8R8G8B8, so the display engine decodes
a 10-bit scanout buffer as 8-bit. GNOME/Mutter picks XRGB2101010 (seen
via drm_info on the ESN20-2TBUD lock screen), which produces the highly
saturated, garbled colors. Advertise 8-bit formats only until the 10-bit
mapping is fixed and tested.

--- a/src/zx_disp.c
+++ b/src/zx_disp.c
@@ -46,10 +46,12 @@
     DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888,
     DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
     DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888,
-    DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010,
-    DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010,
-    DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010,
-    DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010,
+    /*
+     * Do not advertise 10-bit scanout: DrmFormat2CBiosFormat() only maps
+     * ARGB2101010, so XRGB/XBGR/ABGR2101010 fall back to A8R8G8B8 and the
+     * display engine decodes 10-bit pixels as 8-bit, corrupting colors.
+     * Keep 8-bit until the 10-bit mapping is fixed and tested.
+     */
     DRM_FORMAT_YUYV,
     DRM_FORMAT_YVYU,
     DRM_FORMAT_UYVY,
